{"connection_id": "BC-ba500f8bd0e08a369fac", "ref": "WLC:Ps.50.18", "target": "sec17", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Casting instruction behind oneself", "note": "In God’s indictment of people who recite his statutes, the wicked are said to hate discipline and cast God’s words behind them; this makes rejection of instruction a deliberate act, close to the bedbaht’s avoidance."}
