{"connection_id": "BC-903fc1f0a5e9ff5c31c1", "ref": "WLC:Ps.95.7", "target": "sec17", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "The flock summoned to hear God’s voice", "note": "The psalm calls Israel the people of God’s pasture and the sheep of his hand, then says “today, if you hear his voice”; it frames reception of divine speech as the present duty of the addressed community."}
